                        "glosses": [
                            "The yaupon holly, Ilex vomitoria, an evergreen holly shrub with white flowers and red or yellow berries, found in the south-eastern United States."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "66944105-09c8-4ea9-a4c2-cda0aa821280",
                                "sense_id": "2d1ce343-7036-3df2-86c2-b4030a485948",
                                "text": "Yaupon is evergreen like the American holly and the familiar hollies of Christmas decorations, but the leaves of yaupon are small and smooth-edged rather than prickly. Easy to chew and blandly tasty, they would not stand out in a tossed salad."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "571cd2a4-0e8b-4f3f-b627-73f1b26d578f",
                                "sense_id": "2d1ce343-7036-3df2-86c2-b4030a485948",
                                "text": "“I found some yaupon and made some tea. It's North America's only native caffeinated plant. Well, dahoon, but you're not gonna find that in --”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3316546b-e0d4-35b2-b5d5-d4e315c60f79",
                        "entry_id": "8e12224a-2f60-31bd-a726-912dcfb1dea0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tea-like drink, \\\"black drink\\\", brewed from the leaves of this holly (or, sometimes, Ilex cassine)."
                        ],
